IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Part VII, Division 3 of the Interpretation Act 1978 (Northern Territory): General, sections 66A to 72.
-- Reprint as in force at 21 April 2023.
--
-- A function answers JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE where the text itself says yes or no, and NOTHING where it does not.

§ `Section 66A: Gazette publication`

-- If an Act requires a statutory instrument to be published in the Gazette, it is sufficient compliance if the instrument is notified in the Gazette and the notification states the place where copies may be purchased or obtained.
-- The text says that this is enough; it does not say that nothing else is enough, so a case that fails the test is not covered.
-- src:854 | (1) If an Act requires a statutory instrument to be published in the Gazette, it is sufficient compliance with the requirement if:
-- src:855 | (a) the instrument is notified in the Gazette; and
-- src:856 | (b) the notification under paragraph (a) states the place where copies of the instrument may be purchased or obtained.
@ref s 66A(1) (src:854-856)
GIVEN `the instrument is notified in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notification states the place where copies of the instrument may be purchased or obtained` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 66A(1): the requirement that the instrument be published in the Gazette is satisfied` MEANS
    IF   `the instrument is notified in the Gazette` AND `the notification states the place where copies of the instrument may be purchased or obtained`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `Kind of place where copies may be obtained` IS ONE OF
    `a physical place`
    `a website`
    `another publicly accessible electronic format`
    `a place of some other kind`

-- The place may be a website or another publicly accessible electronic format.
-- src:857 | (2) The place under subsection (1)(b) may be a website or another publicly accessible electronic format.
@ref s 66A(2) (src:857)
GIVEN place IS A `Kind of place where copies may be obtained`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 66A(2): the place may be the kind of place` MEANS
    CONSIDER place
    WHEN `a website` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `another publicly accessible electronic format` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `Section 67: tabling documents`

-- A document is tabled in the Legislative Assembly under an Act if it is tabled under the Standing Orders, or delivered to the Clerk and recorded in the Minutes of Proceedings.
-- src:859 | (1) A document is tabled in the Legislative Assembly under an Act if the document is:
-- src:860 | (a) tabled in the Assembly under the Standing Orders of the Assembly; or
-- src:861 | (b) delivered to the Clerk of the Assembly and recorded in the Minutes of Proceedings of the Assembly.
@ref s 67(1) (src:859-861)
GIVEN `it is tabled in the Assembly under the Standing Orders of the Assembly` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is delivered to the Clerk of the Assembly` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is recorded in the Minutes of Proceedings of the Assembly` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 67(1): the document is tabled in the Legislative Assembly under the Act` MEANS
    JUST (`it is tabled in the Assembly under the Standing Orders of the Assembly`
          OR (`it is delivered to the Clerk of the Assembly` AND `it is recorded in the Minutes of Proceedings of the Assembly`))

-- The document must be tabled under subsection (1) within the period specified in the Act.
-- src:862 | (2) The document must be tabled under subsection (1) within the period specified in the Act.
@ref s 67(2) (src:862)
GIVEN `it is tabled under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which it is tabled` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the period specified in the Act` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 67(2): the document is tabled within the period specified in the Act` MEANS
    JUST (`it is tabled under subsection (1)` AND Day `the day on which it is tabled` AT MOST Day `the last day of the period specified in the Act`)

-- If the Act provides for a specified person to table the document, it may be tabled by anyone acting for the person.
-- src:863 | (3) If the Act provides for a specified person to table the document, the document may be tabled by anyone acting for the person.
@ref s 67(3) (src:863)
GIVEN `the Act provides for a specified person to table the document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person tabling it is acting for the specified person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 67(3): the document may be tabled by the person` MEANS
    IF `the Act provides for a specified person to table the document` AND `the person tabling it is acting for the specified person` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- In section 67, Act includes the Northern Territory (Self-Government) Act 1978 (Cth).
-- src:865 | Act includes the Northern Territory (Self-Government) Act 1978 (Cth).
@ref s 67(4) "Act" (src:865)
GIVEN `the Act is the Northern Territory (Self-Government) Act 1978 (Cth)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 67(4) "Act": the Act is within an Act` MEANS
    IF `the Act is the Northern Territory (Self-Government) Act 1978 (Cth)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- In section 67, document includes a report and a statutory instrument.
-- src:866 | document includes a report and a statutory instrument.
@ref s 67(4) "document" (src:866)
GIVEN `it is a report or a statutory instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 67(4) "document": the thing is within a document` MEANS
    IF `it is a report or a statutory instrument` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§ `Sections 68 to 72`

-- Strict compliance with the forms prescribed by or under an Act is not necessary, and substantial compliance, or such compliance as the circumstances of the case allow, is sufficient.
-- src:868 | Strict compliance with the forms prescribed by or under an Act is not necessary and substantial compliance, or such compliance as the circumstances of a particular case allow, is sufficient.
@ref s 68 (src:868)
GIVEN `the form is prescribed by or under an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the compliance is substantial, or as much as the circumstances of the case allow` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 68: strict compliance with the form is necessary` MEANS
    IF `the form is prescribed by or under an Act` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

@ref s 68 (src:868)
GIVEN `the form is prescribed by or under an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the compliance is substantial, or as much as the circumstances of the case allow` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 68: the compliance with the form is sufficient` MEANS
    IF `the form is prescribed by or under an Act` AND `the compliance is substantial, or as much as the circumstances of the case allow` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- If money is due under an Act, it is recoverable in a court or tribunal having, in the Territory, civil jurisdiction to the extent of the amount due.
-- A court whose civil jurisdiction has a monetary limit reaches the amount due only if the limit is at least that amount.
-- src:870 | If money is due under an Act, the money is recoverable in a court or tribunal having, in the Territory, civil jurisdiction to the extent of the amount due.
@ref s 69 (src:870)
GIVEN `money is due under an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount due` IS A NUMBER
      `the monetary limit of the civil jurisdiction of the court or tribunal in the Territory, if it has one` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 69: the money is recoverable in the court or tribunal` MEANS
    IF   `money is due under an Act`
    THEN CONSIDER `the monetary limit of the civil jurisdiction of the court or tribunal in the Territory, if it has one`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST limit THEN
             IF limit AT LEAST `the amount due` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
    ELSE NOTHING

-- A court, judge, justice of the peace, officer, commissioner, arbitrator or other person or body authorised by law or consent of parties to hear and determine a matter has authority to receive evidence and examine on oath any witness appearing before it.
-- src:872 | A court, judge, justice of the peace, officer, commissioner, arbitrator or other person or body authorised by law or consent of parties to hear and determine any matter, has authority to receive evidence and examine on oath any witness appearing before the court, person or body.
@ref s 70 (src:872)
GIVEN `the person or body is authorised by law or by consent of the parties to hear and determine the matter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 70: the person or body has authority to receive evidence and examine on oath any witness appearing before it` MEANS
    IF `the person or body is authorised by law or by consent of the parties to hear and determine the matter` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- An Act may be amended or repealed in the session of the Legislative Assembly in which it was passed.
-- src:874 | An Act may be amended or repealed in the session of the Legislative Assembly in which it was passed.
@ref s 71 (src:874)
GIVEN `the amendment or repeal is made in the session of the Legislative Assembly in which the Act was passed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 71: the Act may be amended or repealed` MEANS
    IF `the amendment or repeal is made in the session of the Legislative Assembly in which the Act was passed` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- All laws and statutes of England, to the extent that they relate to the observance of, or actions permitted or prohibited on, a Sunday, have no force or effect in the Territory.
-- src:876 | (1) It is hereby declared that all laws and statutes of England, to the extent that they relate to the observance of or actions that are permitted to be carried out or prohibited on a Sunday (however described), have no force or effect in the Territory.
@ref s 72(1) (src:876)
GIVEN `it is a law or statute of England` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it relates to the observance of, or to actions that are permitted to be carried out or prohibited on, a Sunday (however described)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 72(1): the law or statute of England has force or effect in the Territory to that extent` MEANS
    IF `it is a law or statute of England` AND `it relates to the observance of, or to actions that are permitted to be carried out or prohibited on, a Sunday (however described)` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- Except as provided by or under a law of the Territory or the Commonwealth, it is lawful to do any act on a Sunday if the act would otherwise be lawful.
-- src:877 | (2) Except as provided by or under a law of the Territory or of the Commonwealth, it is lawful to do any act on a Sunday if the act would be otherwise lawful.
@ref s 72(2) (src:877)
GIVEN `the day is a Sunday` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act would otherwise be lawful` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a law of the Territory or of the Commonwealth provides otherwise for the act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 72(2): it is lawful to do the act on that day` MEANS
    IF   `a law of the Territory or of the Commonwealth provides otherwise for the act`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the day is a Sunday` AND `the act would otherwise be lawful` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
